# Frontend UI Components

- Use shadcn/ui components for interface elements in the client and admin apps. Compose them to build page-specific UI.
- Check the current app for an existing component before using it. If a needed component is missing, follow that app's shadcn/ui setup and add-component workflow, then import it through the configured alias.
- Add a custom UI component only when shadcn/ui does not provide a suitable building block.
- Do not assume shadcn/ui is initialized. Check for the app's `components.json` and dependencies; initialize it following the Next.js existing-project guide before adding shadcn/ui components when needed.
